// This file is a REFERENCE ONLY — Claude Code never reads a ".template" file.
// It exists so the commented instructions survive in git history and on disk,
// since real settings.local.json must be valid JSON (no comments allowed there).
//
// How to activate:
//   1. Create a fine-grained PAT at https://github.com/settings/personal-access-tokens
//      scoped to ONLY this repo, with "Contents: Read/Write" (+ "Pull requests:
//      Read/Write" and "Issues: Read/Write" if Claude should open PRs/comment).
//   2. Copy the JSON block below into the real settings.local.json (same folder).
//   3. Paste your token in place of the placeholder.
//   4. Confirm settings.local.json is listed in .gitignore (it should be already)
//      so this never gets committed.
//
// gh and git both check the GH_TOKEN environment variable automatically —
// that's why setting it here is enough; nothing else needs to reference it.

{
  "env": {
    "GH_TOKEN": "github_pat_REPLACE_WITH_YOUR_REPO_SCOPED_TOKEN"
  }
}
